-- title:
--   Formal coordinates along a section of a formally smooth algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $A$ a commutative $R$-algebra that is formally smooth over $R$, and let $e : A \to R$ be an $R$-algebra homomorphism, with kernel $I = \ker e$. Let $g$ be a natural number and $x : \mathrm{Fin}\, g \to A$ a tuple of elements of $A$ with $e(x_i) = 0$ for every $i$, so that all $x_i$ lie in $I$, subject to two conditions: $I$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the $x_i$ and $I^2$, and the only tuple $c : \mathrm{Fin}\, g \to R$ of scalars with $\sum_i c_i \cdot x_i \in I^2$ is $c = 0$. Then for every commutative $R$-algebra $C$, every ideal $J \subseteq C$ that is nilpotent as an element of the semiring of ideals of $C$, and every tuple $c : \mathrm{Fin}\, g \to C$ with $c_i \in J$ for all $i$, there is a unique $R$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : A \to C$ such that $\varphi(a) \in J$ whenever $e(a) = 0$, and $\varphi(x_i) = c_i$ for every $i$.
--
--   The two hypotheses on the tuple $x$ say that the classes of the $x_i$ generate $I/I^2$ and are $R$-linearly independent there; the conclusion is the functor-of-points form of the statement that the completion of a formally smooth algebra along a section with free conormal module is a formal affine $g$-space with coordinates $x_1,\dots,x_g$, lifts of the section to a nilpotent thickening $(C,J)$ corresponding bijectively to tuples in $J^g$. It is the input used by [`GoodReductionJacobian.RelativeGroupLaw.exists_mvFormalGroup_kernelOfReduction_of_smooth`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.RelativeGroupLaw.exists_mvFormalGroup_kernelOfReduction_of_smooth) to produce the formal group law of a smooth group scheme along its unit section.
